 "max_tier": 5,
 "ai": "normal",
 "intro": [
  "The short road to the Wound runs through Elderwold, the forest the Concord felled to feed its foundries. Nothing grows there now but stumps and thorn. The Thornwood Covenant has not forgotten, and its huntmaster, Neve Hollowreed, has had archers in the stumps for a week.",
  "Maelis was born in this forest. She is quiet the whole way in.",
  "Tier 5 is open: lantern priests heal your army. While the Covenant holds all three of its towns, its archers come out of the tree line again and again. Take Thornmere and Rootholm, then Briarhall."
 ],
 "outro": [
  {
   "if": {
    "flag": "oathbreaker"
   },
   "text": [
    "Briarhall falls. A dying druid tells Maelis what the forest knew: the great roots of Elderwold held the Lockstone in place. When the Concord cut the trees, it cut the seal.",
    "He looks at Maelis and calls her Branwen, and then he looks past her at the smoke over Heartwood and does not say anything else. She does not tell Aldous any of it for a day."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": [
    "Briarhall falls. A dying druid tells Maelis what the forest knew: the great roots of Elderwold held the Lockstone in place. When the Concord cut the trees, it cut the seal.",
    "Before he dies the druid looks at Maelis and calls her Branwen. She does not answer to it, and she does not tell Aldous any of it for a day."
   ]
  }
 ],
